# BAD INPUT on purpose: a CALL whose callee is an array literal that is NOT
# the typed empty-array constructor. `[T]()` (single type-spelled element,
# zero args) IS a valid typed empty-array constructor as of 2026-08-17 -- see
# doc/08_tracking/bug/typed_empty_array_constructor_rejected_2026-08-10.md --
# so this fixture uses a TWO-element array literal, which is never intercepted:
# it stays an ordinary array literal referencing the undefined variable
# `no_such_symbol_here`, which is then CALLED. The interpreter must diagnose
# this (`variable 'no_such_symbol_here' not found` / `not callable`); the seed
# JIT must diagnose too, never crash and never fail open.
fn main():
    var x = [no_such_symbol_here, 2]()
    print("SHOULD_NOT_PRINT")
main()
